    {
      "id": "500c5213-52e3-43cb-b97b-a5198bea12b9",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        14016,
        2640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## AI Study Planner - Detailed & Realistic\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives a study-planning request through Telegram, extracts exam details with Gemini, and checks whether enough information was provided. If details are missing, it asks the user to clarify; otherwise it reads existing plans from Google Sheets, generates a realistic daily study plan with AI, saves it, sends today’s tasks back to Telegram, and logs the activity.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Telegram bot credentials for the trigger and message-sending nodes, and make sure the bot can access the target chat.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for both LangChain chat model nodes.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the correct spreadsheet and sheet/tab IDs for reading existing plans, saving study plans, and logging activity.\n- Review the Set nodes for expected fields such as chat_id, request, subject, exam_date, chapters, hours_per_day, today_message, and activity log values.\n- Verify the structured output parser schemas match the AI prompts for exam-detail extraction and daily-plan generation.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the AI prompts, parser schemas, study-plan fields, and Google Sheets columns to match your preferred planning style, subjects, and reporting format."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5823f78c-c1a1-4416-b56e-ffef057d5c20",
